  "note": "Election of the aldermen of the new Enniskillen Borough Council in 1949: the four Unionist aldermen for the East and South Wards were returned unopposed on 4 May, and the two North Ward aldermen were polled on Wednesday 25 May. The councillors are in the borough's own record (enniskillen-borough-council, 1949); filed apart, as for Belfast and Londonderry (round-2 final, 7 Nov 2026). The Unionist nominations for the East and South Wards are printed together, the aldermen apart from the councillors but without a ward for each, so the two wards are recorded as one area. Returned unopposed."
